# Rust / Cargo build outputs
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rlib

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase-0 parity artifacts: KEEP the docs, scripts, inventory, baseline,
# corpora, goldens, and gate tools. Ignore only generated / compiled outputs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Differential example outputs (regenerated from corpora)
/.port/phase-0/examples-out/

# Compiled differential-harness binaries (the reference oracle driver etc.).
# The harness SOURCE (vt_driver.c, *.sh, *.py, fixtures, DESIGN.md) is KEPT.
/.port/phase-0/harness/**/bin/
*.dSYM/
.port/phase-0/harness/bin/

# Common compiled-binary extensions anywhere under the harness
/.port/phase-0/harness/**/*.o
/.port/phase-0/harness/**/*.a
/.port/phase-0/harness/**/*.so
/.port/phase-0/harness/**/*.dylib

# Reference-oracle BUILD outputs under baseline/ (regenerable; large).
# KEEP: BASELINE.json, METHODOLOGY.md, run_benchmarks.py, raw/ results+logs,
#       and corpora/ (the benchmark input goldens).
# IGNORE: the Zig compilation cache and the compiled reference install tree
#         (the ghostty-bench / ghostty-gen binaries + libs/headers).
/.port/phase-0/baseline/bench-rf-cache/
/.port/phase-0/baseline/bench-releasefast/

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Zig build cache / outputs for harness-only generators (e.g. the rustty-unicode
# differential oracle). KEEP the .zig source + build.zig + build.zig.zon; IGNORE
# the regenerable compilation cache and install tree.
.zig-cache/
**/.zig-cache/
/.port/phase-0/harness/**/zig-out/
# Root zig-out/ resource tree — the macOS Copy-Resources share/ folders, fully
# regenerable via `cargo run -p xtask -- resources`.
/zig-out/

# Phase-0 benchmark corpora (Goal-2 perf baseline): regenerable via the recipe in
# .port/phase-0/baseline/METHODOLOGY.md (deterministic `ghostty-gen`/rustty-synthetic
# seeds). Not needed for the parity gates; kept out of history to stay lean.
/.port/phase-0/baseline/corpora/*.bin

# perf-new7 benchmark corpora: regenerable via the recipe in
# .port/phase-2/perf-new7/RESULTS.md (rustty-synthetic, fixed seeds/sizes).
# Same rationale as the phase-0 corpora above.
/.port/phase-2/perf-new7/corpora/*.vt

# rustc/Miri ICE crash dumps (transient; appear under heavy parallel Miri load)
rustc-ice-*.txt

# regenerable G4 differential per-case output
.port/phase-0/harness/results/diag/
rust_out

# macOS app: regenerable via `cargo run -p xtask -- xcframework`; build output.
# (The bundle is `RusttyKit`, not `GhosttyKit` — R2. The old spelling was left
# behind by the rename and matched nothing.)
macos/RusttyKit.xcframework/
macos/build/
macos/DerivedData/

# regenerable xcframework output (cargo run -p xtask -- xcframework-vt).
# NOT all of dist/ — dist/cmake, dist/doxygen (and dist/linux|windows|macos)
# are checked-in source assets.
#
# The APP bundle is `macos/RusttyKit.xcframework` (ignored above), not this
# directory: that is where Rustty.xcodeproj links it from, matching the
# reference's `GhosttyXCFramework.zig` out_path. The stale `dist/` spelling is
# kept here so an older working tree does not resurface one as untracked.
/dist/RusttyKit.xcframework/
/dist/rustty-vt.xcframework/
# The staged header dirs are per-module (xcframework-headers-RusttyKit,
# -RusttyVt); the bare name is the pre-parameterization spelling, kept so an
# older working tree does not resurface it as untracked.
/dist/xcframework-headers/
/dist/xcframework-headers-*/
# SwiftPM build output for example/swift-vt-xcframework.
example/swift-vt-xcframework/.build/
# Source tarball produced by `cargo run -p xtask -- dist`
# Source tarballs from `xtask dist` / `xtask dist-lib-vt`. The second pattern
# is NOT redundant: `librustty-vt-*` does not match `rustty-*`, and without it
# a 43 MB artifact gets committed.
/dist/rustty-*.tar.gz
/dist/librustty-vt-*.tar.gz

# llvm coverage profiling artifacts
*.profraw

# Nix build results — `nix build` drops a `result` symlink (and `result-<name>`
# for multi-output derivations) in the invocation directory, and the NixOS test
# driver writes an interactive-history file. Both became reachable when the
# flake landed; the reference ignores them for the same reason.
/result*
/.nixos-test-history

# Valgrind core dumps. G-VALGRIND runs every workspace crate's test binaries
# under memcheck, and a crash there leaves one of these behind.
vgcore.*

# SDD scratch (ledger, briefs, reports, review diffs) — not tracked
.superpowers/

# CMake wrapper build dir (cmake -B build-cmake) + Doxygen output — regenerable
/build-cmake/
/doc/

# CMake example build dirs (example/c-vt-cmake*/build)
example/**/build/

# Agent worktrees (transient; each is its own git checkout)
.claude/worktrees/

# WS10: stashed bench binaries for the paired self fence (large, regenerable).
/.perf-bins/

# Restored Zig dependency caches (.port/tools/restore_zig_deps.sh materializes these
# from hash-pinned tarballs; they are downloads, not sources).
**/zig-pkg/

# Miri lane run logs (large, regenerated per run; findings are committed in FINDINGS.md)
.port/phase-3/miri/*.log

.port/codex/**
# !.port/codex/**/
# !.port/codex/**/*.md

# codex-vet remediation ledger: keep the state/designs/scripts, drop caches
.port/codex-vet/__pycache__/

# flatpak-builder outputs (regenerable):
#   flatpak run org.flatpak.Builder --force-clean --user \
#     --repo=flatpak/repo flatpak/builddir flatpak/io.airely.rustty.yml
/flatpak/builddir/
/flatpak/repo/
/flatpak/.flatpak-builder/
.flatpak-builder/

# snapcraft output
/*.snap
/parts/
/stage/
/prime/

# The reference's own .gitignore rules that the sections above do not already
# cover (P-1 parity audit). Editor/dev-environment cruft, the direnv state that
# `.envrc`'s `use flake` / `source_env_if_exists .envrc.local` create, an
# in-source CMake configure, the nix/vm disk image, and the reference's test
# output names (renamed).
*~
*.log
# ...except the committed .port/ run logs (e.g. .port/phase-0/test-run.log);
# the Miri lane logs stay ignored by the rule above, which is re-applied below.
!/.port/**/*.log
.port/phase-3/miri/*.log
.vscode/
.direnv/
.envrc.local
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
example/*.wasm
test/rustty
test/cases/**/*.actual.png
/Box_test.ppm
/Box_test_diff.ppm
/rustty.qcow2
/sprite_face_test*

# rustty-xev wasi_file test fixture (left behind when the test aborts under wasmtime)
wasi-test-file.txt
